Library late loading: do not put deferred relative pointers in TLS images.

RELR is applied by DT_INIT after the loader has copied TLS for existing
host threads. Use an integer loader sentinel, a null default thread-name
pointer and lazy construction of the polymorphic thread-type manager.
NoDestructor avoids TLS destructor registration requiring glibc 2.18.
The engine regression audits the packed TLS relocations and runs its
loop on both main and pre-existing worker threads after dlopen.

--- a/base/threading/platform_thread.cc
+++ b/base/threading/platform_thread.cc
@@ -35,8 +35,11 @@
 }
 
 internal::ThreadTypeManager* GetThreadTypeManager() {
-  constinit thread_local internal::ThreadTypeManager thread_type_manager;
-  return &thread_type_manager;
+  // A constinit polymorphic object puts its vtable in the TLS image. With
+  // packed relocations, copies made for existing dlopen host threads retain
+  // that unrelocated pointer. Construct it on first use in zeroed TLS.
+  thread_local NoDestructor<internal::ThreadTypeManager> thread_type_manager;
+  return thread_type_manager.get();
 }
 
 }  // namespace
